---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import ButtonLink from "./button-link.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "./arrow-icon.astro";
import StainedGlassImg from "../assets/images/stained-glass.jpg";
---

<section class="py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="shell grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] lg:gap-20">
    <figure class="order-last mx-auto w-full max-w-sm lg:order-none lg:max-w-none">
      <div class="arched-frame aspect-[4/5] bg-came">
        <Image
          src={StainedGlassImg}
          alt="A medieval cathedral window of blue and red stained glass"
          widths={[400, 800]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 38vw, 90vw"
          class="size-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-4 text-center text-sm italic text-faint">
        Cathedral glass made 800 years ago still holds its color.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="grid gap-6">
      <p class="eyebrow text-gilt">Why stained glass</p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl leading-[1.1] sm:text-5xl">
        Paint fades. <span class="text-crimson-light">Glass does not.</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="prose-measure grid gap-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        <p>
          Granite has withstood the test of time because it is impervious to
          weather and normal wear in the cemetery. Unfortunately, the paint or
          stain used to enhance the letters, numbers and designs on today’s
          granite has a life expectancy of 2 to maybe 8 years.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground">
          Simply put, stained glass will never fade. We installed our first
          glass inlay in 2003, and we have tested our inlays to extremes that
          monuments will never face. In some ways, the finished product is even
          tougher than the carved granite itself.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="mt-2 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border bg-border sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="grid gap-1 bg-card p-6">
          <dt class="eyebrow">Paint or stain</dt>
          <dd class="font-display text-3xl tabular-nums">2 to 8 years</dd>
          <dd class="text-sm text-faint">before it needs repainting</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-1 bg-card p-6">
          <dt class="eyebrow text-gilt">Stained glass</dt>
          <dd class="font-display text-3xl">Never fades</dd>
          <dd class="text-sm text-faint">the color is fused through the glass</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <ButtonLink href="/product" variant="gilt" size="lg" class="mt-2 w-fit">
        Learn more about our glass
        <ArrowIcon />
      </ButtonLink>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
